# Thousand-Year Storm: "copy it for each other instant and sorcery spell you've cast before it this turn." Only YOUR instants and
# sorceries are counted: on turn 5 Bot1 casts Ornithopter (a creature spell) and Bot2 answers with its own Lightning Bolt - neither
# counts. Bot1 then casts Chain Lightning, a sorcery: copied for none. A Lightning Bolt cast next is copied for exactly one - the
# sorcery counts as much as an instant. The copy is not cast (CR 707.10), so it triggers nothing: one Storm trigger for each of the
# two spells cast. Bot2 takes 3 + 3 + 3 = 9 (11 left); Bot2's Bolt took Bot1 to 17.

